    description: "# Proposal: persist CFG / DDG / receiver-hints as a source-derived sidecar\n\n## Motivation\n\nToday the CFG/DDG/reaching-defs/receiver-hints machinery is built only inside\n`cmd_verify_claims` (via `_build_python_ddg_for_verify_claims` in `cli.py`)\nand discarded at process exit. Each `verify-claims` invocation rebuilds it\nfrom scratch. There is also no way to ask \"show me the CFG for function X\"\nor \"show me the DDG edges in caller Y\" without re-running verify-claims with\n`--json` and parsing the output (and even then, only the verdicts are\nexposed — CFG/DDG remain unreachable).\n\nThe behavior-map JSON (`hypergumbo.results.json`) intentionally does NOT\ncontain CFG/DDG today. Folding them in would (a) force CFG construction\nonto the default `hypergumbo` / `hypergumbo run` path (currently\nsub-second, sketch-oriented, LLM-facing), (b) inflate the JSON\nsignificantly (one CFG per function — ~2700 on hypergumbo itself), and\n(c) strain the ADR-0023 relationship-axis edge taxonomy (CfgNode/CfgEdge\naren't relationship edges).\n\nA **layered cache** keeps the default path fast and the taxonomy clean\nwhile still avoiding the rebuild-every-time waste.\n\n## Sketch\n\n### On-disk layout\n\n```\n~/.cache/hypergumbo/\n└── <repo-fp>/results/<source-fp>/<config-fp>/\n    ├── hypergumbo.results.json         # behavior map (existing)\n    ├── hypergumbo.results.{4,16,64}k.json\n    ├── hypergumbo.results.slices/\n    └── hypergumbo.intra.json           # NEW: CFG + DDG + receiver hints\n```\n\nSame `<source-fp>` directory → same invalidation trigger as the behavior\nmap. The sidecar is source-derived only; it does NOT depend on the\nclaims YAML or the taint sources/sinks/sanitizers catalogs.\n\n### Schema (rough)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"generated_at\": \"...\",\n  \"source_fingerprint\": \"...\",\n  \"stable_id_scheme\": \"...\",\n  \"languages_covered\": [\"python\"],\n  \"cfgs\": {\n    \"<symbol_id>\": {\n      \"language\": \"python\",\n      \"entry\": \"B0\",\n      \"exit\": \"Bexit\",\n      \"blocks\": [\n        {\"id\": \"B0\", \"kind\": \"entry\", \"span\": {...}},\n        {\"id\": \"B1\", \"kind\": \"stmt\", \"span\": {...},\n         \"node_type\": \"assignment\", \"defines\": [\"x\"], \"uses\": [\"y\"]},\n        ...\n      ],\n      \"edges\": [\n        {\"src\": \"B0\", \"dst\": \"B1\", \"kind\": \"seq\"},\n        {\"src\": \"B2\", \"dst\": \"B3\", \"kind\": \"true\"},\n        {\"src\": \"B2\", \"dst\": \"B4\", \"kind\": \"false\"},\n        {\"src\": \"B5\", \"dst\": \"B1\", \"kind\": \"loop_back\"},\n        ...\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"ddg_edges\": [\n    {\"caller\": \"<symbol_id>\", \"var\": \"x\", \"def_line\": 11, \"use_line\": 13}\n  ],\n  \"external_hints\": {\n    \"<caller_symbol_id>\": {\"11:get\": \"os.environ\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Design choices\n\n- **Keyed by Symbol ID**, not flat list — O(1) lookup for \"give me the\n  CFG of symbol X.\"\n- **Symbol IDs are the behavior-map's IDs**; no new ID scheme.\n- **`languages_covered` is explicit** so absence is observable (Python-only\n  today; without this field, a missing CFG is indistinguishable from \"no\n  control flow exists\").\n- **`external_hints` reuses what `taint_refine.py` already produces** and\n  currently throws away.\n- **No taint findings.** Those depend on the claims YAML + extra catalogs\n  and would go stale the moment the user changes their trust zones.\n\n### Producer & consumer paths\n\nProducers:\n1. `verify-claims` writes the sidecar as a byproduct on first build; reads\n   it on subsequent runs (verify-claims becomes near-free when CFG is\n   current — only taint propagation reruns).\n2. New `hypergumbo intra` subcommand for explicit warm-cache and as the\n   debugging entry point. Mirrors `hypergumbo run` alongside `hypergumbo`\n   (sketch).\n\nConsumers enabled:\n- `hypergumbo cfg <symbol>` — print CFG (text or DOT)\n- `hypergumbo ddg <symbol>` — print def-use chains\n- `hypergumbo explain <symbol>` could optionally include CFG summary\n- Future interprocedural analyses, summarization passes, or\n  context-sensitive slicing get a precomputed substrate.\n\n## Open design questions\n\n1. **Size.** Probably MB-scale on a 300k-LOC repo. JSON to start; if it\n   ever crosses \"obnoxious to load,\" switch to JSONL keyed by symbol_id\n   and stream. Don't pre-optimize.\n2. **Language coverage cliff.** CFG builder is Python-only on the\n   production path today. Persisting it makes the gap visible — a feature\n   (honesty) but a new UX surface that needs the \"language not yet\n   supported\" messaging right, or users will read empty CFGs as \"no\n   control flow exists here.\"\n3. **`function_summaries/` overlap.** That module already derives\n   summaries from DDG+CFG. Folding them into the same sidecar (under a\n   `summaries` key) is the natural integration — they're co-derived,\n   co-invalidated, and queried together. Or keep them separate. Decide\n   before implementation.\n\n## Out of scope for this item\n\n- Persisting taint findings (claim-dependent; ephemeral by design).\n- Persisting claim verdicts (same).\n- Folding CFG/DDG into the relationship-axis Edge stream (would violate\n  ADR-0023 and bloat the default-path JSON).\n- Extending CFG language coverage beyond Python (separate concern; this\n  item only proposes persistence of what already exists).\n\n## Origin\n\nDiscussed 2026-05-19 in a familiarization Q&A about hypergumbo's\nintegration model. The conclusion was: the call graph + AST-stamped\ndataflow are already unified in the Edge stream; the CFG and DDG are\nnot, and that's the right separation for the default path — but\npersistence of CFG/DDG belongs on the table as a separate enhancement."  # fe02
